"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:119 — `_review_plan_body` calls `rebar.llm.review_plan(ticket_id, ref=ref, source=source, sign=..., emit_sidecar=..., force=force)` with no `runner=`","Default runner resolution is `runner or get_runner(cfg)` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:488, floors.py:81/184, workflow/gate_dispatch.py)","Existing async MCP tests monkeypatch `rebar.llm.review_plan` ENTIRELY with a fake (tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py:404 `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm, \"review_plan\", fake)`) — which replaces the REAL review and so cannot be used by test 4, which needs the real find/verify/decide passes to produce a genuine own BLOCK","Every other test in test_plan_review_reuse.py injects the fake via the `runner=` parameter, which the MCP path does not expose"],"finding":"Test 4 ('test_gate_status_keeps_run_verdict_apart_from_stale_attestation') does not specify how the `_CountingGateFake` runner reaches the review invoked through the MCP `review_plan_start` tool. The MCP path (`_review_plan_body`) calls `rebar.llm.review_plan(ticket_id, ...)` with NO `runner=` argument, resolving the runner internally via `runner or get_runner(cfg)`; there is no runner-injection parameter on that path, so the fake runner cannot reach the real review unless the test monkeypatches the `get_runner` default-runner seam.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4e3ac44946aa20b4","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 ('start a review through the MCP `review_plan_start` tool with `rebar.llm.review_plan` bound to the real review and the BLOCK runner')","norm_id":"nf4e6532f66362166","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wires test 4 the way existing async MCP tests do (replacing `review_plan`) and the review never runs the real passes — the BLOCK is fabricated by the stub, so the test no longer proves the run's own 14-chunk review blocked on its own finding, defeating the stated purpose","Implementer cannot find a runner-injection seam and the test cannot be written as specified without monkeypatching an unnamed internal (`get_runner`)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 4, specify: monkeypatch `rebar.llm.runner.get_runner` (or the import site used by the plan-review orchestrator) to return the `_CountingGateFake(block=True)`, leaving `rebar.llm.review_plan` as the real function, then call `review_plan_start` and poll `gate_run_status`. This keeps the real find/verify/decide passes while forcing the BLOCK.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary"